WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:05.349
There's an old saying: always be yourself…
unless you can be Batman.

00:00:05.349 --> 00:00:06.329
"What are you?!"

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:09.150
"I'm Batman."

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.679
But not everyone who's considered for the
role of Batman gets the chance, and not everyone

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.549
who's offered the chance actually takes it.

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:18.250
Over the years, a lot of stars have been considered
for the role of the caped crusader for both

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:22.010
television and film, and a lot of fans have
been left wondering what might have been.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:25.429
Here's a look at some actors who were almost
cast as Batman.

00:00:25.429 --> 00:00:26.429
Cillian Murphy

00:00:26.429 --> 00:00:32.200
For his 2005 reboot Batman Begins, director
Christopher Nolan saw as many as a dozen up-and-coming

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.200
actors.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.440
Among them was Irish actor and 28 Days Later
star Cillian Murphy.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.440
He recalls having an "awkward" audition and
screen test in which he read his lines while

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.239
wearing a complete Batman suit.

00:00:42.239 --> 00:00:46.001
He didn't get that part, but Nolan was impressed
enough with his performance that he cast him

00:00:46.001 --> 00:00:47.670
in Batman Begins as the Scarecrow.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.739
Seems like a pretty good choice.

00:00:49.739 --> 00:00:50.969
Josh Hartnett

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:54.969
Josh Hartnett was one of the actors Nolan
considered early on to star in Batman Begins.

00:00:54.969 --> 00:00:59.270
But Hartnett, one of the biggest young male
stars of the early 2000s, pulled his own name

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:03.510
from consideration out of fears he would be
typecast as a superhero, a decision he told

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.720
Playboy that he greatly regrets now.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.940
"Watching Christian Bale go on to do so many
other things has been just awesome.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:11.120
I mean, he’s been able to overcome that.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.160
Why couldn’t I see that at the time?"

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:14.160
Armie Hammer

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.950
In 2007, Warner Bros. was all set to film
a Justice League movie, and though they already

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:22.980
had a Batman in the form of Christian Bale,
director George Miller decided to cast someone

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.010
else in the role.

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:28.820
That someone: Armie Hammer, three years before
his breakout appearance in The Social Network.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:31.980
Justice League ended up being scrapped due
to the Writers Guild of America strike, which

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:32.980
Hammer told Yahoo!

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.720
Movies he's actually grateful for.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.670
"I would have made a terrible Batman.

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:37.700
Really terrible.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:38.700
It's too young.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.200
No-one wants to see a 19-year-old Batman.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.700
What can a 19-year-old do?

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:45.140
It'd be like his parents had just been shot
last weekend."

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.230
Josh Brolin

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:50.570
The No Country for Old Men and Jonah Hex star
met with Man of Steel director Zack Snyder

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:53.880
when it was decided that the plans for the
next Superman movie would include Superman

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.650
fighting the Dark Knight.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:59.610
After that concept morphed into Batman vs.
Superman: Dawn of Justice, Snyder and Brolin

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:03.540
ultimately both decided it wasn't a good fit,
and Brolin moved on to the Marvel universe

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:06.260
as their ultimate boogeyman, Thanos.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:07.260
Wes Bentley

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.719
As Batman vs. Superman took shape, former
Batman boss Christopher Nolan suggested his

00:02:11.719 --> 00:02:14.349
Interstellar star Wes Bentley for the role.

00:02:14.349 --> 00:02:18.489
Best known for American Beauty, The Hunger
Games, and American Horror Story on TV, Bentley

00:02:18.489 --> 00:02:20.069
ultimately was passed over.

00:02:20.069 --> 00:02:21.590
"What do you mean?"

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.480
Instead, Ben Affleck got the role.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.900
Poor Ben...

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.000
Bill Murray

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.310
It sounds crazy, but back in the mid-80's,
Ghostbusters director Ivan Reitman was amongst

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:34.540
a handful of directors considered by Warner
Bros. to develop a big-screen vehicle for

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:35.540
Batman.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:36.629
Reitman's choice for the lead role?

00:02:36.629 --> 00:02:40.260
Ghostbusters star Bill Murray, with Eddie
Murphy reportedly in the running as Robin.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:44.019
With the comic book version of Batman enjoying
a revival thanks to grim and gritty stories

00:02:44.019 --> 00:02:47.510
like The Dark Knight Returns, though, Warner
Bros. ultimately opted against the comedic

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:50.980
route in favor of Tim Burton's dark and manic
vision.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.299
Pierce Brosnan

00:02:52.299 --> 00:02:55.819
The future James Bond was on director Tim
Burton's short list for the role of the Dark

00:02:55.819 --> 00:02:58.650
Knight in his 1989 film version of Batman.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:02.510
But as the actor explained in a Reddit AMA,
he met with Burton and just couldn't see himself

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:04.670
in the role because he thought it was all
rather silly, saying:

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:09.099
"Any man who wears his underpants outside
his pants just cannot be taken seriously."

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:14.400
And it'd be a shame for Brosnan to do anything
that couldn't be taken seriously.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:23.290
Not to mention how preposterous the Batmobile
is, right?

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:24.719
Ray Liotta

00:03:24.719 --> 00:03:29.389
Ray Liotta had just starred in his first movie
— Something Wild, in 1986 — when his agent

00:03:29.389 --> 00:03:32.859
got a call saying Tim Burton was interested
in auditioning him for the lead role of Batman.

00:03:32.859 --> 00:03:36.920
He declined even the chance to meet with Burton,
something he says he still regrets.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.469
Don't feel too sorry for Liotta, though.

00:03:38.469 --> 00:03:41.849
He opted to make the Oscar-nominated classic
Goodfellas instead.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.980
"Ahahhahaha!"

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.029
Alec Baldwin

00:03:46.029 --> 00:03:49.530
No less a film authority than Quentin Tarantino
once said that Alec Baldwin would have made

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.749
a great Batman in the 1980s.

00:03:51.749 --> 00:03:53.069
And it almost happened!

00:03:53.069 --> 00:03:56.931
Like Pierce Brosnan, Baldwin was being considered
for Tim Burton's Batman, having worked with

00:03:56.931 --> 00:03:59.200
the director on his previous movie, Beetlejuice.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.010
But another Beetlejuice star, Beetlejuice
himself, Michael Keaton, wound up with the

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:06.340
part, making Baldwin one of the ultimate what-ifs
in Batman history.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:09.060
"You're working with a professional here!"

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:13.359
He did get a consolation prize though: the
lead role in the 1994 flop The Shadow, which

00:04:13.359 --> 00:04:15.819
he's still trying to get people to forget.

00:04:15.819 --> 00:04:17.190
William Baldwin

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:21.340
When both director Tim Burton and star Michael
Keaton opted to not return for the third Batman

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:24.540
movie, new director Joel Schumacher was hired
to helm Batman Forever.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:27.480
And he brought along his own ideas about who
should star.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:33.480
His choices: Ralph Fiennes, Daniel Day-Lewis,
Val Kilmer, and William "Billy" Baldwin, Alec's

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:34.480
younger brother.

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:36.540
"Hey hey quick question Jack: our underwear?

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:41.541
Is it regular black bikini cut or is it silk
boxers with Tweety Bird on em, cause I have

00:04:41.541 --> 00:04:42.541
both."

00:04:42.541 --> 00:04:45.550
Baldwin auditioned for Schumacher, who told
him that he'd been the first choice…but

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.420
that Warner Bros. executives preferred Val
Kilmer.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:52.040
Billy eventually got his day in the sun voicing
Batman for several animated projects.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:05:00.480
"We both looked into the abyss, but when it
looked back at us, you blinked."

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.200
David Duchovny

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:06.620
Like Michael Keaton before him, Val Kilmer
walked away from the cape and cowl after Batman

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:07.620
Forever.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:10.200
"Can I persuade you to take a sandwich with
you sir?"

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.850
"I'll get drive-thru."

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:15.880
Warner Bros. had to scramble to find an actor
to star in 1997's Batman &amp; Robin.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:19.660
The choice came down to two emerging TV stars:
George Clooney of ER and David Duchovny of

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:21.030
The X-Files.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:24.790
Clooney ultimately got the role...and promptly
put the franchise into a decade long deep

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:25.790
freeze.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:28.280
"No sign of the snow man."

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.770
"Maybe he melted."

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:31.750
"No, he's just hibernating."

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:34.360
Looks like Duchovny had the last laugh.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.360
Lyle Waggoner

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:39.880
Finally, no Batman list would be complete
without a look at the 1966 TV series.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:43.940
When ABC was putting together the campy classic,
producers looked at potential Batmen and Robins

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:44.940
as duos.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:45.940
"Holy multitudes!"

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:51.340
The final two options came down to Lyle Waggoner
and Peter Deyell, or Adam West and Burt Ward.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:55.020
West and Ward got the parts, of course, while
Waggoner went on to co-star on The Carol Burnett

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:56.020
Show.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:57.020
Who knows how this one would've turned out?

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:58.820
If Waggoner had won the role, the show might
have bombed.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.580
"Somedays you just can't get rid of a bomb!"

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:03.590
Thanks for watching!

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.150
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:09.389
And leave us a comment to let us know which
of these stars would have made the best Batman…

